{{Short description|none}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=May 2018}}
'''Group 1 of the [[1966 FIFA World Cup]]''' consisted of [[Uruguay national football team|Uruguay]], hosts [[England national football team|England]], [[France national football team|France]], and [[Mexico national football team|Mexico]]. Play began on 11 July 1966 and concluded on 20 July 1966. England won the group and Uruguay finished as runners-up, and both advanced to the quarter-finals. Mexico and France failed to advance. England went on to win the tournament.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Stokkermans |first1=Karel |last2=Jarreta |first2=Sergio Henrique |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tables/66f.html |title=World Cup 1966 (England, July 11–30) |website=RSSSF.com |publisher=[[Rec.Sport.Soccer Statistics Foundation]] |date=22 October 1999 |access-date=26 May 2018}}</ref>

